  {
   "id": 529701,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/5d172d9571c66849.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Gerardo Poli/VetTimes)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The provided graph shows an oxygen dissociation curve for hemoglobin.</p>\n<p>If the carbon dioxide concentration in the environment is increased, how will this affect the curve?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1036740,
     "content_html": "The curve will become more flat."
    },
    {
     "id": 1036741,
     "content_html": "The curve will become taller."
    },
    {
     "id": 1036742,
     "content_html": "The curve will shift towards the right."
    },
    {
     "id": 1036743,
     "content_html": "The curve will shift towards the left."
    }
   ],
